Auto run the shell

The professional way to auto-run this without prompts is using Task Scheduler.

Step 1: "Install" the Script
Create a folder on your C: drive, for example: C:\Tools\DefenderCenter.

Save the script code as DefenderCenter.ps1 inside that folder.

Step 2: Set up Auto-Run (The Clean Way)
This method uses Windows Task Scheduler to launch the tool with "Highest Privileges" automatically when you log in, skipping the annoying Yes/No prompt.

Press Windows Key + R, type taskschd.msc, and hit Enter.

On the right side, click Create Task.

General Tab:

Name: Defender Command Center

Security Options: Check "Run with highest privileges" (Critical!).

Configure for: Select Windows 10.

Triggers Tab:

Click New.

Begin the task: Select "At log on".

Click OK.

Actions Tab:

Click New.

Action: Start a program.

Program/script: powershell.exe

Add arguments: -WindowStyle Hidden -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "C:\Tools\DefenderCenter\DefenderCenter.ps1" (Make sure the path matches where you saved it!)

Click OK.

Conditions Tab:

Uncheck "Start the task only if the computer is on AC power" (so it runs on laptops too).

Click OK.

Step 3: Create a Desktop Shortcut (Optional)
If you want a desktop icon to launch it manually:

Right-click your Desktop > New > Shortcut.

Paste this into the location box: powershell.exe -WindowStyle Hidden -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "C:\Tools\DefenderCenter\DefenderCenter.ps1"

Click Next, name it "Defender Center", and click Finish.

(Optional) Right-click the new shortcut > Properties > Change Icon and pick a shield icon to make it look official.
